I think it was me, and the context was different: it was an early
/wishing.  In that case, getting SDSM and then waiting until you have
40 HP and getting an MR-granting artifact (or CoMR) makes sense, since
you _know_ that you can get MR before you start needing it (golden
nagas, levelports, polytraps, liches, titan, etc).

But if you get one early wish (a magic lamp, smoky potion djinni, etc)
then I'd definitely go for GDSM because you have a 75% chance of
finding reflection by medusa.

Yes, /lightning, /fire, etc will suck in the interim.  Make sure you
level up fast so that they're not instadeath (with the DSM you
certainly have the AC to support levelling up quite a bit).

> >#7: Do not drink from fountains until you're CERTAINLY you can handle
> >the effects!
>
> Bingo. I always leave fountains alone or generally more effectively turn
> them into pools by digging into an out of the beaten path one.
>
> In fact I need to remember to use later game fountains like thrones.

Save the ones on higher dungeon levels, pickaxe out a lower one.
Higher DLs have much greater chance of granting a wish.

And once you can safely handle the moccasins/nymphs/water daemon, DO
NOT QUAFF!  #dip items in them (if you have something you want
uncursed, that's great).

The "this water's no good" message sucks no matter how tough you are
(randomly curses your inventory).  You can't get it from #dipping, only
#quaffing.  And the benefits of drinking are almost never enough to
offset the penalties.

