> >Jackal: These deaths are probably from overwhelmed newbies, but jackals
> >can be dangerous to 1st level characters.
>
> Again the "one more hit" mentality. Jackals are pet fodder until the
> pet maxes out.

Except while you're still XL1, when you want the XP for yourself.  The
first few XLs add dramatically to your HP and survivability. After XL2
the 1XP monsters aren't worth as much and you can leave them to the
pet, but very early on you want to take them down yourself.

> >Small mimic: The best way to handle these is to be careful in shops and
> >build a strong pet.  Still, they're slow enough that often you can
> >melee one to death.
>
> While in pre protection mode, I literally lead them out of the shop and
> let them re-mimic outside the shop. You almost never have to melee them
